":"Good! Now I have the schemas:\n- For farmers_markets: I need to sum the `farmers_markets` column, excluding territories\n- For census_population: I need to get the 2025 population from the 'United States' row, which should be in the `NAME` column with value `'United States'` and the `POPESTIMATE2025` column\n\nLet me first peek at the data to understand the structure better, then create a metric that will calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents. I'll use the cross-dataset pattern from the skill: create a build script that reads both sources and joins them.\n\nFirst, let me explore the farmers_markets data to see what states are included and understand what territories might be.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me explore the data to find the total farmers markets (excluding territories) and the US population:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01UB3uRnFzqDBsxYGswAJxm8","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.select('state_name', 'farmers_markets').limit(60)"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01YUte3W2GvTxtSrKKAukGjk","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"census_population","compose":"source.filter(source.NAME == 'United States').select('NAME', 'POPESTIMATE2025')"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":412,"cacheRead":18589,"cacheWrite":1465,"totalTokens":20480,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.00206,"cacheRead":0.0018589000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.00183125,"total":0.005764150000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":167},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786911984120,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74CGw2n6Etn6SGRuHeY","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01UB3uRnFzqDBsxYGswAJxm8","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_name\",\"farmers_markets\"\n\"California\",647\n\"New York\",555\n\"Pennsylvania\",426\n\"Minnesota\",390\n\"Illinois\",370\n\"Virginia\",336\n\"Wisconsin\",335\n\"Michigan\",321\n\"Massachusetts\",273\n\"Florida\",246\n\"Georgia\",231\n\"Ohio\",219\n\"Texas\",216\n\"Missouri\",208\n\"North Carolina\",196\n\"Iowa\",194\n\"Kentucky\",183\n\"Indiana\",181\n\"Colorado\",164\n\"Washington\",159\n\"Maryland\",140\n\"Connecticut\",124\n\"Kansas\",123\n\"Oregon\",122\n\"Alabama\",115\n\"Oklahoma\",102\n\"Arizona\",97\n\"Tennessee\",95\n\"South Carolina\",86\n\"New Jersey\",84\n\"Montana\",78\n\"Arkansas\",77\n\"Louisiana\",73\n\"Vermont\",71\n\"Alaska\",59\n\"Idaho\",59\n\"West Virginia\",57\n\"Wyoming\",57\n\"Nebraska\",55\n\"District Of Columbia\",54\n\"New Hampshire\",50\n\"Mississippi\",49\n\"Delaware\",49\n\"Maine\",43\n\"New Mexico\",34\n\"Rhode Island\",33\n\"Utah\",30\n\"Nevada\",28\n\"North Dakota\",18\n\"South Dakota\",17\n\"Hawaii\",13\n\"Puerto Rico\",2\n\"Virgin Islands\",0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786911990713},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01YUte3W2GvTxtSrKKAukGjk","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"NAME\",\"POPESTIMATE2025\"\n\"United States\",341784857\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786911990713},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see that:\n1. The farmers_markets data includes states and territories (Puerto Rico has 2 markets, Virgin Islands has 0)\n2. The US population is 341,784,857\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Sum all the farmers_markets from the farmers_markets table, excluding Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands (the territories)\n2. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n\nLet me create a build script that creates the metric. I'll sum all farmers_markets from the farmers_markets table excluding the territories (Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands).","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I'll create a build script to calculate the metric of farmers markets per 100,000 residents:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01TFLJpXWGsTJLbvmEbQTssf","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census_population\",\n    storage_options=so\n)\n\n# Sum farmers markets excluding territories (Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands)\nfact_total = (\n    fact.filter(\n        (fact.state_name != \"Puerto Rico\") & (fact.state_name != \"Virgin Islands\")\n    )\n    .aggregate(total_farmers_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum())\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Get US population\ndenom = (\n    ref.filter(ref.NAME == \"United States\")\n    .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\")\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Join and calculate metric\nexpr = (\n    fact_total.join(denom, fact_total.k == denom.k)\n    .mutate(\n        farmers_markets_per_100k=(\n            fact_total.total_farmers_markets / denom.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000\n        )\n    )\n    .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"farmers_markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":758,"cacheRead":20054,"cacheWrite":811,"totalTokens":21637,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0037900000000000004,"cacheRead":0.0020054,"cacheWrite":0.00101375,"total":0.006823150000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":133},"stopReas